cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ClaimSem in your research, please cite this software."
title: "ClaimSem: Structure-Aware Claim Aggregation for Patent Clustering"
type: software

authors:
  - given-names: "Yongmin"
    family-names: "Yoo"

version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-16"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Yongmin-Yoo/claimsem"
url: "https://github.com/Yongmin-Yoo/claimsem"

license: "MIT"

keywords:
  - "patent NLP"
  - "patent clustering"
  - "claim dependency"
  - "claim embeddings"
  - "structure-aware pooling"
  - "spherical K-means"
  - "Cooperative Patent Classification"

abstract: >-
  ClaimSem is a lightweight method for constructing patent-level
  representations from individual patent claims. It encodes claims
  separately with a frozen patent language model and aggregates them
  using independent-claim emphasis and dependency-depth decay. The
  resulting patent representations are reduced using a development-fitted
  PCA transform and clustered using spherical K-means.
